# README - Queue Operations

## Aim
This folder contains queue-related programs that demonstrate the basic operations of a queue using different implementations.

---

## Algorithm
1. Create a queue and initialize it as empty.
2. For the STL queue version, push elements into the queue and remove the front element using pop.
3. For the linked-list version, add nodes at the rear and remove nodes from the front.
4. Check whether the queue is empty and display the contents when needed.

---

## How it works
A queue follows the FIFO (First In, First Out) principle. The first inserted element is removed first. In the linked-list version, the front pointer points to the first node and the rear pointer points to the last node.

---

## Functionality
- Insert an element into the queue
- Remove the front element
- Check whether the queue is empty
- Display the contents of the queue

---

## Time and Space Complexity
- Enqueue / Dequeue: O(1) average
- Display: O(n)
- Extra space: O(n) for the linked-list version and queue storage
